From b307ecda0934863bfa1e88c56131df64d6836ce8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Schiffhauer <alexander.schiffhauer@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 23:59:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] winewayland.drv: Add StatusNotifierItem tray support.

Wayland has no XEmbed system tray selection, so the icons explorer docks
are invisible when winewayland.drv is the desktop driver. Publish every
docked icon as a StatusNotifierItem on the session bus instead.

The driver dlopens libdbus and keeps one private session bus connection
in the desktop process. Every docked icon claims an
org.kde.StatusNotifierItem-<pid>-<serial> name, all of them share one
object path, and the name a host addresses selects the item.

The connection is dispatched from a Wine thread which the first dock
insert starts through a user mode callback, so other processes never
create it. Activation methods only post a private driver window message
to the icon's adaptor window, and the Win32 tray callbacks then run on
Wine's message path from the explorer thread.

Explorer keeps owning the item lifetime: dock insert creates an item or
updates it in place, and dock remove releases it. When the
StatusNotifierWatcher changes owner, e.g. because the shell restarted,
the driver registers its items again and asks explorer to re-dock, like
the X11 driver does when a tray manager appears. Losing the bus
connection unpublishes the items and asks explorer to re-dock as well,
which reconnects.

WINE_SNI_ICON_NAME, read once at driver init, sets the IconName
property so that hosts can show a themed icon instead of the pixmap.

Signed-off-by: Alexander Schiffhauer <alexander.schiffhauer@gmail.com>
